  "goodToKnow": "Der Kanzlerkandidat or die Kanzlerkandidatin is a party's candidate for chancellor. Legally, voters elect the Bundestag, which then elects the chancellor, but the main parties name candidates who lead their campaigns. The debate over who will run is called die K-Frage. It's a weak noun: den, dem, des Kanzlerkandidaten. Plural: die Kanzlerkandidaten."
